## 6. Build Commands

⚠️ **Not covered in this tutorial.** The page does not show explicit `pip install` or `python setup.py` commands. It states only that extensions are "built 'ahead of time' with setuptools" (vs. "just in time" via `load_inline`), and directs readers to the [extension-cpp repository](https://github.com/pytorch/extension-cpp) for the complete build setup. For actual build commands, consult that repo or the [cpp_extension docs](https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/cpp_extension.html) (standard practice would be `pip install .` / `python setup.py develop`, but that is not stated on this page).

